From f1d91efa46ce1c226cd636d879bf2517a9ef4d80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:39:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(sim): simulate and verify external NC programs
 against the setup

Add camcraft_app::nc_sim. It takes a program that camcraft-gcode parsed
and simulates it against the setup:
- maps each T number to cutter geometry (an explicit map, the document's
  tool numbers, or a .camtools row) and refuses unmapped numbers by name;
- maps program coordinates to world millimetres (origin + sign * program,
  with the WCS flip and the machine's inverted axes; arcs reverse sense
  when one in-plane axis is negated);
- cuts the setup stock with the dexel engine and measures the deviation
  from the target model; refuses a setup with no stock by name;
- runs verify::solid_hits, bands_vs_fixtures_held and
  rapids_vs_fixtures_held, and the machine travel, feed, spindle and tool
  size limits, each finding on its 1-based NC line;
- builds a PlaySeed (PlaySeed::of_planned) so the playback can run it.

camcraft-app now depends on camcraft-gcode; the decision record is
docs/decisions/2218-nc-sim-runner.md.

Fixes #2218

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
